        <p class="member__lead">Sanaa Syed is our Patient Care Coordinator and your first point of contact at Meaningful Psychiatry, and we are so happy to have her on our team!</p>

        <h3>How Sanaa Helps</h3>
        <p>From your very first call or message, Sanaa is here to make getting care feel simple and supported. She walks new patients through every step of getting started, answers questions along the way, and keeps communication between patients and providers clear and timely, so you can focus on your care rather than the paperwork.</p>
        <p>Sanaa can help you with:</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Scheduling and rescheduling appointments</li>
          <li>New patient intake and onboarding paperwork in the Osmind patient app</li>
          <li>Insurance and billing questions</li>
          <li>Prescription refill requests and messages for your provider</li>
          <li>General questions about our services and what to expect</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Background</h3>
        <p>Sanaa is currently a first-year medical student and an aspiring psychiatrist. She holds a B.S. in Informatics (Biomedical &amp; Health Systems) and a minor in Bioethics from the University of Washington Seattle. Before joining Meaningful Psychiatry, she gained hands-on experience in patient services and care coordination at Kaiser Permanente, worked in behavioral health with children and families at Kids and Family Counseling, and supported clinical teams at UW Medicine and Seattle Children’s Research Institute.</p>

        <p class="member__closing">Sanaa brings warmth, patience, and care to every interaction, and she is committed to making sure every patient feels welcomed and heard from the very first hello.</p>
